## Code wiki

The root README and `{{wiki_dir}}/` are a code wiki for people, checked against the code by a lint.

- **To fix or change code, search the code first.** Do not read wiki pages to get oriented. Open one section where it saves a search: the README for the set-up, run and test commands; "When it goes wrong" in `{{wiki_dir}}/howto/run-and-debug.md` for an error or a symptom; `{{wiki_dir}}/reference/map.md` for the file behind a behaviour you could not find (one row per module, then the known traps); `{{wiki_dir}}/index.md` to find a written explanation. `grep -rn "<words of the report>" {{wiki_dir}}` costs less than reading a page.
- **A change that alters behaviour, setup, commands or layout updates the wiki in the same change.** Fix the pages `python {{tools_dir}}/wiki.py affected` lists. Append `## [YYYY-MM-DD] change | <title>` and a line `Updated: <pages>. Checked: <pages still true>.` at the end of `{{wiki_dir}}/log.md`. Run `python {{tools_dir}}/wiki.py lint --strict` (after a diagram edit, `python {{tools_dir}}/wiki_browser.py render` first; add `--run --clean-env` when setup or commands changed).
- A new page or diagram follows `{{wiki_dir}}/SCHEMA.md`; a routine update does not need that file. Wiki pages never change code.
